 studies of dairy product and calcium intakes and prostate cancer risk: a meta-analysis</article-title><source>J Natl Cancer Inst</source><year>2006</year><volume>98</volume><fpage>794</fpage><lpage>795</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Natl Cancer Inst||98|794||bib9|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16757704</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tuohimaa</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Tenkanen</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Ahonen</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Lumme</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Jellum</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Hallmans</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Stattin</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Harvei</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hakulinen</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Luostarinen</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Dillner</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Lehtinen</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hakama</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Both high and low levels of blood vitamin D are associated with a higher prostate cancer risk: a longitudinal, nested case&#x02013;control study in the Nordic countries</article-title><source>Int J Cancer</source><year>2004</year><volume>108</volume><fpage>104</fpage><lpage>108</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Int J Cancer||108|104||bib10|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14618623</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>